   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to peace officers employed by Cornell University; and to repeal subdivision 59 of section 3 of such law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S2859",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2859-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §3 sub 59, amd §3-b, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2859\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public officers law, in relation to\npeace officers employed by Cornell University; and to repeal subdivision\n59 of section 3 of such law relating thereto\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:  To allow for Cornell University, Itha-\nca campus to hire campus police officers who live outside of Tompkins\nCounty.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill repeals amendments made by a chapter of the laws\nof 2012 amending the public officers law, as proposed in S.7485-A.\nSection two of the bill adds a new subdivision in section 3-b of the\npublic officers law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  In order to improve hiring, and allow for greater free-\ndom of residency location, the legislation would allow for Cornell\nUniversity police officers, who are assigned to the Ithaca campus, to\nreside outside of Tompkins County, and still perform their official\nfunctions at the university.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: Undetermined.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  Immediately; provided that section one of this act\nshall take effect on the same date as a chapter of the laws of 2012\namending the public officers law relating to residency requirements for\npeace officers employed by Cornell University, as proposed in legisla-\ntive bills numbers S.7485-A and A.10400-A, takes effect.\n\n",
